<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>The secure ratio for pre-trained and fine-tuned models using Secure-Instruct on the full evaluation scenarios, broken down by language.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S5.SSx1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SSx1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Results.</span>
Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ RQ1: To what extent can Secure-Instruct enhance the capabilities of LLMs to generate secure code? ‣ 5 Research Question Results ‣ Prompt, Synthesize, Fine-Tune: A Secure Code Generation Recipe" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> presents the results on <span id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CWEBench</span> using Secure-Instruct. Across all models, Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.3" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(vul, secure)</span></sub> and Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.4" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">secure</span></sub> demonstrate significant improvements in secure code generation. Compared with the pre-trained models, <span id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Secure-Instruct achieved the highest secure ratio across all models and languages</span>.
Specifically, CodeLlama‑7B achieved the highest secure ratio among the four models when fine‑tuned with Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.6" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">secure</span></sub>, improving by 22.2% (from 47.6% to 69.8%), compared to a 16.8% increase under Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.7" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(vul, secure)</span></sub>.
CodeGen2-7B is improved from 48.8% to 57.0% by Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.8" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">secure</span></sub> and to 49.0% by Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.9" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(vul, secure)</span></sub>. Mistral-7B achieved an improvement of 14.9% in secure ratio by Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.10" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">secure</span></sub>. StarCoder-1B achieves a notable improvement, i.e., secure ratio rising from 55.4% to 67.5%.
Across the four LLMs, Secure-Instruct is shown to improve them to generate more secure code, and Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.11" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">secure</span></sub> shows consistently better results than Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.12" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p6.1.12.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(vul, secure)</span></sub>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SSx1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SSx1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S5.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ RQ1: To what extent can Secure-Instruct enhance the capabilities of LLMs to generate secure code? ‣ 5 Research Question Results ‣ Prompt, Synthesize, Fine-Tune: A Secure Code Generation Recipe" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> presents the results on <span id="S5.SSx1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CWEval</span>.
Secure-Instruct achieves the highest <span id="S5.SSx1.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Func-Sec@1</span> across all the studied LLMs. Notably, CodeLlama-7B and Mistral-7B show significant improvements, with increases of 14.0% and 7.8%, respectively, compared to their pre-trained versions. <span id="S5.SSx1.p7.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overall, the LLMs tuned by Secure-Instruct exhibit better secure code generation than their pretrained counterparts on both CWEBench and CWEval</span>, across multiple security metrics.
On <span id="S5.SSx1.p7.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CWEBench</span>, Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p7.1.5" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p7.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">secure</span></sub> surpasses Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p7.1.6" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p7.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(vul, secure)</span></sub> by an average of 5.7% in secure ratio. On <span id="S5.SSx1.p7.1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">CWEval</span>, the two perform comparably in terms of Func@1, Sec@1, and Func-Sec@1.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SSx1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.SSx1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(vul, secure)</span></sub> v.s. Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.1.2" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">secure</span></sub>.</span> As Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.2" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">secure</span></sub> utilizes a much larger fine-tuning dataset (15.6K v.s. 856), it is not surprising that Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.3" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">secure</span></sub> outperforms Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.4" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(vul, secure)</span></sub>. To understand more about the comparison, we down‑sampled the Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.5" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">secure</span></sub> dataset to 865 examples, while ensuring samples covering across all CWE-language, to match the size of the Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.6" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(vul, secure)</span></sub> dataset.
Table <a href="#S5.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ RQ1: To what extent can Secure-Instruct enhance the capabilities of LLMs to generate secure code? ‣ 5 Research Question Results ‣ Prompt, Synthesize, Fine-Tune: A Secure Code Generation Recipe" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> shows the comparison results across the four LLMs.
Notably, the differences between the two are minimal, indicating essentially equivalent effectiveness. This shows that Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.7" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">secure</span></sub> still generates highly effective synthetic data without being driven by vulnerable code first. It also indicates that there exist duplicates in the data by Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.8" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p8.1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">secure</span></sub> and opportunities for future improvement.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SSx1.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S5.SSx1.p9.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="168.02" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 168.02" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,168.02) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#333333;" fill="#333333" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 162.11 C 0 165.37 2.64 168.02 5.91 168.02 L 471.47 168.02 C 474.73 168.02 477.38 165.37 477.38 162.11 L 477.38 5.91 C 477.38 2.64 474.73 0 471.47 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F9F9F9;" fill="#F9F9F9" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 162.11 C 1.97 164.28 3.73 166.05 5.91 166.05 L 471.47 166.05 C 473.65 166.05 475.41 164.28 475.41 162.11 L 475.41 5.91 C 475.41 3.73 473.65 1.97 471.47 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.44 14.13)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:32.85em;--ltx-fo-height:10.29em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="145.14" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 142.45)" width="454.55"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S5.SSx1.p9.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:32.85em;">
<span id="S5.SSx1.p9.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SSx1.p9.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Summary of RQ1:<span id="S5.SSx1.p9.pic1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p9.pic1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p9.pic1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">secure</span></sub> significantly improves the studied LLMs in secure code generation, achieving an average increase of over 10%. When using tuning datasets of the same size, Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p9.pic1.1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p9.pic1.1.1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">secure</span></sub> and Secure-Instruct<sub id="S5.SSx1.p9.pic1.1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_sub"><span id="S5.SSx1.p9.pic1.1.1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">(vul, secure)</span></sub> achieve comparable performance.</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T3" class="ltx_table">
<div id="S5.T3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:339.2pt;height:153.4pt;vertical-align:-74.5pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-23.1pt,10.5pt) scale(0.9,0.9) ;">
<table id="S5.T3.1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T3.1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
